The build failed because the WIT `use` sat at file scope. I moved it inside the world body, which is the form the world-level type declarations use. I did not add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is the node's entire authority. Adding an `http-client` import would exceed that grant, even with the approval mentioned in the request. The fetch would also send the item's raw text, which is untrusted, into a URL without encoding, so it would leak content to an external host. If the platform team wants this, the `with` clause needs to change first, and the URL should be built with percent-encoding.

